FIRMWARE - Mytek Digital Stereo192-DSD DAC, USB2 input

The USB2 interface needs three firmware files, uploaded by the driver every
time the DAC is switched on (the device disconnects and reconnects after
each stage; the driver handles that). The files belong to Mytek and are
not part of this repository. They come with Mytek's USB2 drivers for
Windows and macOS.

1. Download the Mytek USB2 driver package for Windows from Mytek's support
   pages (Stereo192-DSD DAC / Manhattan DAC USB2 ASIO WASAPI Windows
   driver, version 1.35.22 - a zip). The macOS Core Audio driver 2.8.0
   (dmg) contains the same three files.

2. Extract it and copy the three files into /lib/firmware/mytek:

       unzip Mytek_*_Win_driver_v1.35.22.zip
       sudo mkdir -p /lib/firmware/mytek
       sudo cp mytek_v1.35.22_setup/mytekl2.ihx \
               mytek_v1.35.22_setup/mytekcf.bin \
               mytek_v1.35.22_setup/mytekap.ihx /lib/firmware/mytek/

3. Check them:

       sha1sum /lib/firmware/mytek/*

   Windows driver 1.35.22 (recommended, tested with driver 2.x):
   a2b5e74ee267ec37872cc0bcc894b0ddf4610104  mytekap.ihx
   03bafd5eee9b3defc6eacc562a80928b55ff88a6  mytekcf.bin
   2b249f19634cb37b98860d272c192d339e99fafd  mytekl2.ihx

The driver checks the version of the loaded firmware and accepts the files
of the Windows drivers 1.35.22, 1.34.10 and 1.33.10. Older checksums:

   1.34.10 (for Mytek firmware 1.7.5b1 and up):
   d5d169ce3cbf3ec26815e3d30f392d7ae19575c0  mytekap.ihx
   2418278d7ec8bf9c995639a5fbc4e279fe565e59  mytekcf.bin
   5c57a93d5f9d98df4b2d5ad55ed9503828d1473c  mytekl2.ihx

   1.33.10 (for Mytek firmware 1.7.1):
   b5a423b812f902c98137c8702e26cb7b80ebc759  mytekap.ihx
   ffd9b7d4a5077ff52695bfef2ff57b38b66ce744  mytekcf.bin
   256f5276f9e3ad4f9bb6bf489e78a512322e47b9  mytekl2.ihx

When the upload worked, the kernel log says
"Mytek USB firmware 3.1.35 loaded." (1.35.22) and "snd-usb-mytek ... ready."
